"""Mutation list for spec 022 tasks 36 and 37 (`BE-PAYLOAD-001`, from 060's
and 020's analyses): every `ductus exec` extension request is inline while it
fits `[artifacts] read-size-bytes`; past it, it names the file the host reads
for each body, with `content-form: path`, and, still past it, moves the lists
that grow with entries and its legacy tail to the file `request-lists-file`
names, with each count inline; a body the runtime did not read stays as it
is; a malformed read size halts the build. Each mutation
removes one half of that, and the tests in `interpreter::payload::tests`
kill it. A request reads the read size twice, once where it names its bodies
and once where it moves its lists, so the mutations that swallow a malformed
read size swallow both reads together: either alone leaves the other to halt.

Run with `python3 scripts/mutation/run.py scripts/mutation/exec-requests-bounded.py
[ID ...]`; see run.py for the format. This file is data, read with
ast.literal_eval: keep every value a literal. An id is never reused: a
mutation that no longer applies is removed, and the next one takes the next
free number. When the code a mutation anchors on changes, update the anchor
in the same change; `run.py --check` names every anchor that no longer
matches exactly once.
"""

